think Studied image/convex_hull.rye for the compose-not-braid pattern, the Point type, the exact-integer cross discipline, and the pure-point-set + raster crux split; studied tools/turning_witness.rish for the witness template (native `contains`, never a shell grep -- REDS #85).
think Designed the exact primitive: for each hull edge (Freeman-Shapira 1975 -- the min-area rectangle of a convex polygon is flush with an edge), measure the projection range along the edge and the cross-product range perpendicular to it; area = dot_range * cross_range / edge_len_sq, an exact rational. The WINNING edge is chosen by an EXACT i128 cross-multiplication (area_i = N_i/D_i, compare N_i*D_j vs N_j*D_i) so no float ever picks the wrong supporting edge; only angle, dimensions, and elongation are read in f64 (they divide by a square root), as moments.rye reads orientation.
think Designed the DECISIVE crux before coding as pure integer point sets (following convex_hull's algebraic-crux discipline, since rasterizing a 45-degree edge is jagged): a square tilted 45 degrees fills only HALF its axis-aligned box -- oriented area EXACTLY 8 over an axis 16, strictly below by exact i128 -- the fact regions.rye's upright box cannot make; an upright 6x4 rectangle's oriented box IS its axis box (equal, never below); a tilted 2:1 rectangle reads true orientation (a 45-degree multiple), honest dimensions, and rotation-invariant elongation EXACTLY 2 where the axis box inflates all three.
obs MEASUREMENT BEAT MEMORY: my first exact-area assertions hardcoded the rational num/den (64/8 for the tilt, 32/8 for the bar). The bar tripped BarRectExactAreaWrong on metal -- two hull edges tie at area 4, and the min-selection seats the FIRST tied edge, so the reduced form landed 8/2 not 32/8. The rational value 4 is right; the specific num/den is traversal-dependent. Fixed all exact-area checks to assert the VALUE (num == area * den), tolerance-free and reduction-independent. A tie in a min-selection is a boundary the fixture must respect, not a bug.
obs TAME gate caught a compound assert on the dot/cross bounds (`a and b`) -- split each into two named asserts so a failing half names itself. tame_style_check then GREEN, width-check clean.
